# Security

```python
# ❌ BAD
logger.info("Connecting %s", camera.rtsp_url)

# ✅ GOOD
from src.security import redact_rtsp_url
logger.info("CAMERA_OPEN_FAILED camera=%s url=%s", camera.id, redact_rtsp_url(url))
```

- Real RTSP credentials live in `.env` (gitignored). YAML may reference `${RTSP_URL}` only. Never commit `.env`.
- Dashboard camera payloads omit `rtsp_url`. Do not add it to `CameraRow` or React types.
- Evidence: `resolve_evidence_file()` must stay inside the evidence root. Do not serve arbitrary paths.
- No biometric ID, face crops for recognition, or mapping track IDs to employees.
- V1 has no login — do not expose the dashboard beyond localhost without calling that out. Do not add auth unless asked.
